\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. None is like Jeshurun's God,
\par So great, so strong, so high;
\par Lo! He spreads His wings abroad,
\par He rides upon the sky:
\par Israel is His first-born son;
\par God, the almighty God, is Thine;
\par See Him to thy help come down,
\par The excellence divine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thee the great Jehovah deigns
\par To succour and defend;
\par Thee the eternal God sustains,
\par Thy maker and Thy Friend:
\par Israel, what hast thou to dread?
\par Safe from all impending harms,
\par Round thee and beneath are spread
\par The everlasting arms.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. God is Thine; disdain to fear
\par The enemy within:
\par God shall in thy flesh appear,
\par And make an end of sin;
\par God the man of sin shall slay,
\par Fill thee with triumphant joy;
\par God shall thrust him out, and say:
\par Destrot themall, destroy!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. All the struggle then is o'er,
\par And wars and fightings cease;
\par Israel then shall sin no more,
\par But dwell in perfect peace:
\par All his enemies are gone;
\par Sin shall have in him no part;
\par Israel now shall dwell alone,
\par With Jesus in his heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Blest, O Israel, art Thou!
\par What people is like thee?
\par Saved from sin by Jesus, now
\par Thou art and still shalt be;
\par Jesus is thy sevenfold shield,
\par Jesus is thy flaming sword;
\par Earth, and hell, and sin shall yield
\par To God's almighty Word.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

